-# FH6 Radio Tool v3.0.34 Hotfix
+# FH6 Radio Tool v3.0.35 Hotfix
 
-- Fixed the v3.0.33 portable EXE prompt that incorrectly told users to run `setup_env.bat` for missing `pywinauto`.
-- In the Nexus/Nuitka EXE package, `setup_env.bat` is intentionally not present; running an old v2 setup script cannot repair a compiled EXE.
-- The Nuitka builder now verifies Windows automation dependencies before building and includes `pywinauto`, `comtypes`, `win32com`, and Win32 modules more explicitly.
-- The Nexus package builder no longer copies a separate `ffmpeg.exe` into the final upload ZIP by default.
-- Main-menu music replacement remains fixed to `GLB_RadioPressStart.assets.bank`; users only select the replacement audio.
+- Removed the obsolete user-facing **Auto-control Fmod Bank Tools** checkbox from the normal workflow.
+- One-click replacement, package generation, and main-menu music replacement now force Fmod Bank Tools GUI automation internally.
+- Fixed the legacy path where unchecking the old option could still show a misleading `setup_env.bat` / `pywinauto` prompt in the portable EXE.
+- If automation dependencies are missing in a compiled EXE, the tool now reports it as a bad/old build and asks for v3.0.35 or newer, instead of asking users to run old v2 setup scripts.
+- Main-menu music replacement remains fixed to `GLB_RadioPressStart.assets.bank`; users only choose the replacement music file.
